# Frontend Environment Variables for Vercel

## Development
- Vite dev proxy automatically routes `/api` to `http://localhost:5000`
- No env file needed

## Production (Vercel)
Create these environment variables in Vercel project settings:

```
VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend-url.onrender.com
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
```

Replace `https://your-backend-url.onrender.com` with your actual Render backend URL (without `/api`).

**Google OAuth Setup:**
1. Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com)
2. Create a new project or select existing one
3. Enable Google+ API
4. Go to "Credentials" and create OAuth 2.0 Client ID
5. Add authorized JavaScript origins:
   - `http://localhost:3000` (for development)
   - `https://your-frontend-domain.vercel.app` (for production)
6. Copy the Client ID and use it for VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
7. Use the same Client ID in backend's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID

## Build
```bash
npm run build
```

Vite will automatically inject the env var at build time.
